<title>USA: German stance unchanged if G7 talks currencies.</title>
<headline>German stance unchanged if G7 talks currencies.</headline>
<dateline>DENVER 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The German stance on currency movements will remain unchanged if the subject is debated during the Group of Seven summit here this weekend, a delegation source told reporters.</p>
<p>&quot;I am not sure how much dollar-yen or dollar-mark will play a role,&quot; the source said. &quot;If it is thrown up we will go back to the declaration in principle which finance ministers have made in previous months.&quot;  </p>
<p>G7 finance ministers and central bank chiefs said in April that exchange rates should reflect economic fundamentals, and that excess volatility and significant deviation from fundamental values were undesirable.</p>
</text>
